#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-observe-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"The network-observe interface lets a snap query network status. Covers what "
"read-only means here and which sockets it still allows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-observe-interface.md:8
msgid "network-observe interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-observe-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`network-observe` enables the querying of the network's status, giving "
"privileged read-only access to networking information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-observe-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"'Read-only access' means the snap can't change network settings. It can "
"still open TCP and UDP connections, through the name-resolution rules the "
"interface includes, and raw sockets for `ping`. A snap with `network-"
"observe` connected can therefore reach the network even without the {ref}"
"`network interface <interfaces-network-interface>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-observe-interface.md:14
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""
